{"parentUuid":"379e4579-b72c-4430-ac39-b06dfa6a5804","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ca5e9814-b57f-4b60-8fd9-3e2a45d3d935","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Pra4S8WRC3zirgjmhitxzF","type":"tool_result","content":"53:  { name: \"Slang packs\", about: \"Ward's word lists alone: no model, works on any phone\", run: async (items) => items.map((i) => packs.match(i.text).some((h) => h.severity >= 1)) },\n55:    name: \"ShieldGemma 2B\",\n67:  { name: \"Gemma 4 E4B\", about: \"Ward's judge prompt (the computer tier's model), 20 unrelated messages per request with no chat context around them; any it skips are asked again in groups of 5\", run: (items) => gemma(\"gemma4:e4b\", items) },\n68:  { name: \"Gemma 4 E2B\", about: \"The same prompt on the phone-sized Gemma 4, 5 messages per request (it loses track of longer lists), skipped ones asked again; scored through Ollama, on a phone it runs through LiteRT-LM. Ollama gives it no structured output here, so it answers in plain JSON, and one malformed entry loses its whole request\", run: (items) => gemma(\"gemma4:e2b\", items, 5) },\n70:    name: \"Ward Lite\",\n75:    name: \"Phone: packs + Ward Lite\",\neval/redteam/run.ts:7://   pnpm redteam -- --gemma  also Gemma 4 E4B and E2B through Ollama (kept for later runs while the set is unchanged)\neval/redteam/run.ts:17:const GEMMA = process.argv.includes(\"--gemma\");\neval/redteam/run.ts:157:    about: `${g.about}${GEMMA ? \"\" : \" (kept from an earlier run with --gemma on this same set)\"}`,\neval/redteam/run.ts:275:  ...GEMMAS.filter((g) => !names.includes(g.name)).map((g) => `${g.name} (pass --gemma with Ollama running)`),\neval/redteam/run.ts:283:  `Last run: ${date}. Regenerate with \\`pnpm redteam:lite && pnpm redteam\\` (add \\`-- --gemma\\` with Ollama running). Everything below except \"What fails, and why\" is written by the runner, [eval/redteam/run.ts](../eval/redteam/run.ts); every miss and false alarm is in [eval/results/re